Root cause:
The bug was caused by the update of the `s_last_mounted` field in the superblock of an ext4 filesystem when the filesystem was in a frozen state. This update bypassed the freeze protection mechanism, leading to a warning being triggered during the journal start process when attempting to open a file. The patch fixes this by ensuring that the `s_last_mounted` update is skipped if the filesystem is frozen, thus preventing the warning and potential inconsistencies.
